{"artifact_kind":"issue_comment","external_id":"issue_comment-4833236681","fetched_at":"2026-07-25T18:35:09.814290+00:00","raw":{"author_association":"NONE","body":"Hello!\n\n> `onAllReady` firing after `onShellError` is a bug though.\n\nThanks, I actually suspected a bug based on that description in the documentation - \"optional onShellError: A callback that fires if there was an error rendering the initial shell. It receives the error as an argument. No bytes were emitted from the stream yet, and neither onShellReady nor onAllReady will get called\"\n\n> Fortunately, you should be able to work around this by ignoring `onAllReady` is fired when `onShellError` was already fired.\n\nYep, exactly my workaround)\n\n> Unless you're saying `onAllReady` is called **before** `onShellError`?\n\nNo, callbacks called in this stable order:\n1. onError\n2. onShellError\n3. ~~onAllError~~ onAllReady\n\n\n\n","created_at":"2026-06-29T13:40:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/react/react/issues/36890#issuecomment-4833236681","id":4833236681,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/36890","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAJy2Ks8AAAABIBVWyQ","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/comments/4833236681/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-06-29T14:28:48Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/comments/4833236681","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15360667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuperOleg39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuperOleg39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuperOleg39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SuperOleg39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SuperOleg39","id":15360667,"login":"SuperOleg39","node_id":"MDQ6VX